cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software in academic or research work, please cite it using the metadata below.
  Note: this is a research-only, offline toolkit and makes no alpha claim; see README.md and
  docs/V1_LIMITATIONS.md.
title: "eth-research: an offline, reproducible toolkit for ETH trading-strategy research"
abstract: >-
  A research-only Python toolkit for developing and evaluating Ethereum trading research on historical
  OHLCV data. It runs fully offline with deterministic, canonically-hashed artifacts; it has no live
  trading, exchange/wallet connectivity, network access, leverage, shorting, or derivatives, and makes
  no alpha claim. As of v1.1.0 the repository ships no LICENSE, so it is not cleared for public
  redistribution (see docs/V1_LICENSE_DECISION.md).
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The eth-research maintainers"
version: "1.1.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/panfot1409/gambling-winnings"
keywords:
  - ethereum
  - backtesting
  - quantitative-research
  - reproducible-research
  - offline
